course: dictionary
lesson: 14271
title: Words from history: nobleman
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nobleman is a man from the nobility, the highest social class below the king or queen. You can see the word man inside nobleman, and that is a clue that it is a person. The other clue is the title: a nobleman might be a duke, an earl, a lord or a count.
explain: «The nobleman rode out from his castle with ten knights behind him.» A castle and knights are clues from the story. Nobleman must be a important person, not a servant or a farmer, because he has a castle and knights.
explain: «The farmers who worked the nobleman's land had to give him part of their harvest.» Here the context tells you that noblemen often owned land and had power over the people who worked it. Ask yourself: who has the power in this sentence? The nobleman does.
fact: A nobleman belongs to the nobility, the highest social class below the king or queen.
fact: A nobleman often has a title, such as duke, earl, lord or count.
fact: Noblemen often owned land and castles.
fact: Noblemen had power over the people who worked their land.
fact: In 1215, barons, who were noblemen, made King John agree to Magna Carta.
exercise: «The nobleman rode out from his castle with ten knights behind him.» What is a nobleman? | A servant who cooked the food in the castle | A horse that carried a knight | *A man of high rank who often owned land and castles | A baker who sold bread in the village
exercise: Which of these is a title a nobleman might have? | Farmer | Sailor | Baker | *Duke
exercise: «The farmers who worked the nobleman's land had to give him part of their harvest.» Why did the farmers have to give him food? | Because it was a harvest party | Because he was poor and hungry | Because he was their friend and wanted a gift | *Because he had power over the people who worked his land
test: In 1215 some noblemen, called barons, made King John agree to Magna Carta. Who made King John agree? | The farmers who grew the food | Nobody, the king agreed on his own | The knights' horses | *The noblemen, called barons
test: Where does a nobleman sit in society? | At the very bottom of society | Outside society completely | *Just below the king or queen | Above the king or queen
exam: Which of these is a nobleman? | A sailor who works on a ship | *A duke who owns land and a castle | A child playing in the park | A baker who sells bread
